[{:db/id 17592186083327 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b864ebe6-e085-5252-a91f-4ca0cb314e2f" "question-b9258154-36aa-5bfe-9428-732732589876"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083129 :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $\\left[0, 10\\right],$ compute $P\\left(X \\leq 7\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n![](images/e7/e76831e0e537ad6fdd429115b56034f54f9071574430c41fb9fe5b4888a72b48.svg)\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $\\left[0, 10\\right],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/7a/7a7bfa98d0a54a198c0050e763a2f1ac75bca751063b9ea20ec6979163049c6f.svg)\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 7) & =P(0\\le X\\le 7) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{7}\\frac{1}{10}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7-0}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083321 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2b0137dd-0ad1-53cf-acd8-0bbd632c8d90" "question-f0228a94-8a4a-532e-880c-3c74fb2a7fa3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083123 :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-1, 4],$ compute $P(0<   X <  3).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n![](images/e8/e8a1e7972e4e4a543c2e774894f83ec38755e7b2145a5b301e44906affac9c15.svg)\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-1,4],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/5c/5ca4ceb0bed3882328dbfa8fb54eb9de948a53d66d9850b8d40781d19f50f4fc.svg)\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0<X<3) & =P(0<X<3) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3-0}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083328 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6a51ea05-5e14-5ec8-80f9-413f5ec71214"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083130 :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $Y$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $\\left[1, 16\\right],$ compute $P\\left(Y  \\geq  10\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $Y$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n![](images/64/64661e76a430c63a3ba74d43f3d074e43d5c03a1a09c39d714a087d5fb8b5afa.svg)\n\nOur random variable $Y$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $\\left[1, 16\\right],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n![](images/bd/bd2bfc727ccdaeb4d0912640c12fa99900db52102aefe3a3dce46ad2e2cbfef0.svg)\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y\\ge 10) & =P(10\\le Y\\le 16) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{10}^{16}f(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{10}^{16}\\frac{1}{15}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{16-10}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-b864ebe6-e085-5252-a91f-4ca0cb314e2f" :question/id #uuid "b864ebe6-e085-5252-a91f-4ca0cb314e2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96284" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $U$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-10,10],$ compute $P(U<-3).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $U$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le u\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $U$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-10,10],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20},\\, & -10\\le u\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(U<-3) & =P(-10\\le U<-3) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-10}^{-3}f(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-10}^{-3}\\frac{1}{20}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{-3-(-10)}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-efac0da0-aee9-5e9c-ae73-a7e2c584348e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-efac0da0-aee9-5e9c-ae73-a7e2c584348e" :answer-field/id #uuid "efac0da0-aee9-5e9c-ae73-a7e2c584348e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f8195f95-abed-5f7b-abf8-51d99c4e7df0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1acc037d-bce5-53b6-8323-1b252862f034" "answer-f4a1a7df-15e9-518c-9fce-7ec892fe2232" "answer-af55ac66-d6ee-5c68-93d5-ab774affd010" "answer-f8195f95-abed-5f7b-abf8-51d99c4e7df0" "answer-83a78c2b-ec57-5782-818b-1ebb0a0fb0c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1acc037d-bce5-53b6-8323-1b252862f034" :answer/id #uuid "1acc037d-bce5-53b6-8323-1b252862f034" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4a1a7df-15e9-518c-9fce-7ec892fe2232" :answer/id #uuid "f4a1a7df-15e9-518c-9fce-7ec892fe2232" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af55ac66-d6ee-5c68-93d5-ab774affd010" :answer/id #uuid "af55ac66-d6ee-5c68-93d5-ab774affd010" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8195f95-abed-5f7b-abf8-51d99c4e7df0" :answer/id #uuid "f8195f95-abed-5f7b-abf8-51d99c4e7df0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83a78c2b-ec57-5782-818b-1ebb0a0fb0c3" :answer/id #uuid "83a78c2b-ec57-5782-818b-1ebb0a0fb0c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{20}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b9258154-36aa-5bfe-9428-732732589876" :question/id #uuid "b9258154-36aa-5bfe-9428-732732589876" :question/math-academy-id "q-96279" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[3,10],$ compute $P(W\\le 5).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $W$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le w\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[3,10],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7},\\, & 3\\le w\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W\\le 5) & =P(3\\le W\\le 5) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}f(w)\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{5-3}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d020dc5f-a9e6-5b1f-9ba1-79c84664ccd0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d020dc5f-a9e6-5b1f-9ba1-79c84664ccd0" :answer-field/id #uuid "d020dc5f-a9e6-5b1f-9ba1-79c84664ccd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3f72b617-3a2d-566c-9b4c-88d79b0fb5b9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3feeccff-adf9-5ba7-9142-c8b271570281" "answer-3f72b617-3a2d-566c-9b4c-88d79b0fb5b9" "answer-25c1f749-943c-58ad-b0b0-8e9b295a57ad" "answer-1e99867f-cfc9-54c7-b348-5f78d1c3d9fa" "answer-fe28eeec-5654-567a-b9a6-2676f4eb678e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3feeccff-adf9-5ba7-9142-c8b271570281" :answer/id #uuid "3feeccff-adf9-5ba7-9142-c8b271570281" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f72b617-3a2d-566c-9b4c-88d79b0fb5b9" :answer/id #uuid "3f72b617-3a2d-566c-9b4c-88d79b0fb5b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25c1f749-943c-58ad-b0b0-8e9b295a57ad" :answer/id #uuid "25c1f749-943c-58ad-b0b0-8e9b295a57ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1e99867f-cfc9-54c7-b348-5f78d1c3d9fa" :answer/id #uuid "1e99867f-cfc9-54c7-b348-5f78d1c3d9fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe28eeec-5654-567a-b9a6-2676f4eb678e" :answer/id #uuid "fe28eeec-5654-567a-b9a6-2676f4eb678e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2b0137dd-0ad1-53cf-acd8-0bbd632c8d90" :question/id #uuid "2b0137dd-0ad1-53cf-acd8-0bbd632c8d90" :question/math-academy-id "q-96334" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-3,1],$ compute $P(-2\\le X\\le 2).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-3,1],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}, & -3\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-2\\le X\\le 2) & =P(-2\\le X\\le 1) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1-(-2)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-75e81c82-0d29-5aa1-9b44-d0a62600de34"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-75e81c82-0d29-5aa1-9b44-d0a62600de34" :answer-field/id #uuid "75e81c82-0d29-5aa1-9b44-d0a62600de34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0e3d93ec-eb09-56cb-a416-5e2e7bec5a82" :answer-field/choices ["answer-19f85468-debe-56c4-9c7b-72ce62714596" "answer-4538c02d-cc56-5357-9692-c45dbd1ff415" "answer-eb1915dd-5764-5752-856c-c61ccdaa99f8" "answer-b411a94b-c858-532e-8504-f3fa46b1d90a" "answer-0e3d93ec-eb09-56cb-a416-5e2e7bec5a82"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19f85468-debe-56c4-9c7b-72ce62714596" :answer/id #uuid "19f85468-debe-56c4-9c7b-72ce62714596" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4538c02d-cc56-5357-9692-c45dbd1ff415" :answer/id #uuid "4538c02d-cc56-5357-9692-c45dbd1ff415" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb1915dd-5764-5752-856c-c61ccdaa99f8" :answer/id #uuid "eb1915dd-5764-5752-856c-c61ccdaa99f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b411a94b-c858-532e-8504-f3fa46b1d90a" :answer/id #uuid "b411a94b-c858-532e-8504-f3fa46b1d90a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e3d93ec-eb09-56cb-a416-5e2e7bec5a82" :answer/id #uuid "0e3d93ec-eb09-56cb-a416-5e2e7bec5a82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-f0228a94-8a4a-532e-880c-3c74fb2a7fa3" :question/id #uuid "f0228a94-8a4a-532e-880c-3c74fb2a7fa3" :question/math-academy-id "q-96333" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ compute $P(0\\le X\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2\\pi },\\, & -\\pi \\le x\\le \\pi , \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-0)}{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4d9e477c-a83d-55bd-a460-7bef9eab339b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4d9e477c-a83d-55bd-a460-7bef9eab339b" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d9e477c-a83d-55bd-a460-7bef9eab339b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-19b9c547-b3de-5a3b-af9a-1d4bd21add26" :answer-field/choices ["answer-51df5392-9584-5939-887e-e5eb023f5973" "answer-107d2581-115e-5fcf-a7ba-4b8a4e067792" "answer-33ea49c6-ab8b-5f20-989d-636291cc3105" "answer-19b9c547-b3de-5a3b-af9a-1d4bd21add26" "answer-534fce73-0f67-5e15-aa99-7cc2da173c69"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51df5392-9584-5939-887e-e5eb023f5973" :answer/id #uuid "51df5392-9584-5939-887e-e5eb023f5973" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-107d2581-115e-5fcf-a7ba-4b8a4e067792" :answer/id #uuid "107d2581-115e-5fcf-a7ba-4b8a4e067792" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-33ea49c6-ab8b-5f20-989d-636291cc3105" :answer/id #uuid "33ea49c6-ab8b-5f20-989d-636291cc3105" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-19b9c547-b3de-5a3b-af9a-1d4bd21add26" :answer/id #uuid "19b9c547-b3de-5a3b-af9a-1d4bd21add26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-534fce73-0f67-5e15-aa99-7cc2da173c69" :answer/id #uuid "534fce73-0f67-5e15-aa99-7cc2da173c69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{16}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083967 :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $Y$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-6,-1],$ compute $P(Y>-5).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $Y$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le y\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $Y$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-6,-1],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5},\\, & -6\\le y\\le -1, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y>-5) & =P(-5<Y<-1) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-5}^{-1}f(y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-5}^{-1}\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{-1-(-5)}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186082733 :answer-field/correct 17592186082738 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-6a51ea05-5e14-5ec8-80f9-413f5ec71214" :question/id #uuid "6a51ea05-5e14-5ec8-80f9-413f5ec71214" :question/math-academy-id "q-130692" :question/problem "Given that the continuous random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[0,4],$ compute $P(W\\ge 1).$" :question/worked-solution "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $W$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le w\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[0,4],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4},\\, & 0\\le w\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W\\ge 1) & =P(1\\le W\\le 4) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(w)\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{4-1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-99010428-33fd-5dd7-a898-3d5893398292"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-99010428-33fd-5dd7-a898-3d5893398292" :answer-field/id #uuid "99010428-33fd-5dd7-a898-3d5893398292" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3f1ef539-7e09-5084-96af-05c9d696698e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2e30620f-4add-5a5d-8a10-63fa89353160" "answer-a32c4229-ee76-5056-a461-20d9ac56ae28" "answer-160a5126-2e24-5c1b-be6a-a06e49dea788" "answer-8df8f671-8474-59ab-86d4-5301bd912c5a" "answer-3f1ef539-7e09-5084-96af-05c9d696698e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e30620f-4add-5a5d-8a10-63fa89353160" :answer/id #uuid "2e30620f-4add-5a5d-8a10-63fa89353160" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a32c4229-ee76-5056-a461-20d9ac56ae28" :answer/id #uuid "a32c4229-ee76-5056-a461-20d9ac56ae28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-160a5126-2e24-5c1b-be6a-a06e49dea788" :answer/id #uuid "160a5126-2e24-5c1b-be6a-a06e49dea788" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8df8f671-8474-59ab-86d4-5301bd912c5a" :answer/id #uuid "8df8f671-8474-59ab-86d4-5301bd912c5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f1ef539-7e09-5084-96af-05c9d696698e" :answer/id #uuid "3f1ef539-7e09-5084-96af-05c9d696698e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186084481 :tutorial/content "A continuous random variable $X$ follows a **continuous uniform distribution** on the interval $[a,b]$ if all values of $X$ are equally likely on $[a,b].$\n\nIntuitively, the familiar statement \"choose a random number between $a$ and $b$\" can be translated as \"observe a value from the continuous uniform distribution on $[a,b].$\" \n\nThe probability density function for the continuous uniform distribution on an interval $[a,b]$ takes the following form:\n\n![](images/a2/a247cacd484a99d579d2a30245d7ab495f6d0d116fbf02e2fe8a95fa658df9c6.svg)\n\nThis corresponds to the following graph:\n\n![](images/9d/9d077084b025c673533cefc52b7d2e7bfe90e8f903e926a27ce8d1207a0d4e79.png)\n\nNotice that the probability density of the continuous uniform distribution on $[a,b]$ is just $1$ divided by the length of the interval. This ensures that our probability density function has the same value everywhere in the interval and integrates to $1{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\frac{x}{b-a}|}_{a}^{b} \\\\  & =\\frac{b-a}{b-a} \\\\  & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen a random variable $X$ follows a continuous uniform distribution on the interval $[a,b],$ we often write\n\n$$\nX\\sim U[a,b]\n$$\n\n \n\nand say that \"$X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[a,b].$\"" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083469 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
